      "summary": "An application the person removes (or whose joining they undo, or that another device removed) now takes what it served along: its contracts, header bars and deciders leave the kernel and its windows close, so its window can no longer answer the assistant, which under `assistantGrants: 'all'` it could before. A contract whose module is no longer on the desktop is no one's to call. A kept application is never restored over a contract another module declares. The install sheet opens with Cancel focused, so a stray Enter never consents, and two suites named at once show their sheets one after the other.",
      "id": "consent-fixes"
    },
